LECTURE_EXPANSIONS = [
    "A spectrograph measures wavelength, so redshift begins with line identification and wavelength calibration. For a comoving source and observer in an expanding FLRW spacetime, photon wavelengths scale with the cosmic scale factor during propagation, giving 1+z=a0/ae. Peculiar motion adds a local Doppler component; at low redshift it can dominate the Hubble-flow contribution. The Hubble parameter defines an instantaneous expansion rate, and c/H0 is a characteristic present scale, not the particle horizon or a direct distance to every object.",
    "For radial light propagation, ds=0 in the FLRW metric gives a comoving interval equal to the integral of c dt/a(t), or c dz/H(z). Curvature maps radial comoving distance into a different transverse distance; only in a flat geometry are they equal. Flux dilution and photon-energy/time stretching lead to luminosity distance, while apparent angular size uses angular-diameter distance. Etherington reciprocity links them when photon number is conserved and propagation is metric. Every distance label therefore encodes a measurement operation and assumptions.",
    "A supernova light curve supplies peak flux, color, and temporal width, but standardization is empirical and population-dependent. After corrections, an apparent magnitude still combines absolute luminosity and distance. The distance modulus isolates the luminosity distance only after the calibrated absolute magnitude is specified. Because a uniform shift in absolute calibration can mimic a change in H0, relative distances over redshift constrain the shape of expansion while an external anchor is needed for an absolute scale. The course subset exercises that distinction and intentionally cannot replace the full survey sample.",
    "Let r be the vector of standardized observed magnitudes minus model magnitudes and C their covariance. Correlated calibration modes mean that a residual in one object predicts part of the residual in another. Cholesky factorization C=LL^T permits whitening by solving Ly=r; then chi-square is the squared norm of y. A common intercept can be profiled analytically using the same covariance-weighted solves. The selected block makes that operation tangible, but omitted survey rows, selection and full nuisance treatment prevent generalizing its intercept or chi-square to the parent analysis.",
    "Before baryon drag, pressure in the photon-baryon fluid launches acoustic waves. The maximum propagation distance becomes a preferred comoving separation in later matter clustering. An isotropic analysis averages radial and transverse dilation into D_V, while anisotropic clustering preserves D_M/r_d and H(z)r_d. The ruler's physical length is set by early-universe densities; a late-time distance in Mpc is therefore conditional on its calibration. When using published BOSS summaries, carry the r_d,fid/r_d factor explicitly and do not compare it as an unscaled absolute distance by accident.",
    "The pre-recombination photon-baryon fluid oscillates under gravity and pressure. The angular peak spacing measures a ratio of the sound horizon at last scattering to the comoving angular-diameter distance. The precision of that ratio does not mean every ingredient is late-time or model-independent: baryon loading, radiation content, recombination, curvature and expansion history enter the conversion. A bandpower spectrum has a full covariance and foreground model; a reported parameter summary is not interchangeable with the raw spectra. This package uses the former only as a cited literature result and labels its curve theoretical.",
    "Weak lensing shears background galaxy images through line-of-sight tidal fields. In the thin-lens limit, tangential shear traces the projected surface-density contrast divided by a geometry-dependent critical density. Cosmic shear correlates source shapes; galaxy-galaxy lensing cross-correlates lens positions and source shapes; clustering correlates lens positions. Combining them can calibrate biases but also couples nuisance parameters such as source redshift distributions, intrinsic alignments, shear response, galaxy bias and baryonic structure. S8 compresses a long posterior direction and should be interpreted with its model and covariance, not as sigma8 alone.",
    "In linear theory, density perturbations grow under self-gravity while cosmic expansion damps their motion. The growth equation's friction term depends on H(a), and its source depends on the clustering matter fraction. The logarithmic rate f=d ln D/d ln a links density growth to coherent peculiar velocities; redshift-space anisotropy therefore adds a growth observable to geometric distance measures. The supplied integral solves a scale-independent smooth-dark-energy approximation and normalizes D(0)=1. It excludes radiation, massive-neutrino scale dependence and nonlinear evolution, so its values are model calculations rather than survey measurements.",
    "A likelihood states the probability of data conditional on parameters; a prior encodes information or regularization before the data; the posterior combines both. For correlated Gaussian data, the quadratic residual term must be accompanied by the covariance determinant unless it is constant over the parameters being varied. A contour depends on whether nuisance parameters are fixed, profiled or marginalized, and on parameter coordinates. Published one- or two-dimensional summaries discard much of the joint likelihood and may share calibration or data. Therefore a sum of inverse variances is not a valid multi-probe analysis without a justified independence model.",
    "A catalog is a selected sample, not a transparent window onto the parent population. Detection probability can depend on flux, color, cadence, host background and follow-up resources. Near a flux threshold, more numerous faint sources can scatter upward than bright sources scatter downward, producing Eddington bias; Malmquist bias describes related luminosity-selection effects. The likelihood must account for truncation and selection normalization. A redshift histogram mixes comoving volume, evolution and completeness, so the deliberately target-stratified Pantheon+ excerpt is useful for plotting practice but cannot estimate the survey selection function.",
    "Two experiments disagree only after they estimate the same parameter under compatible assumptions. For a difference, the variance includes both individual variances and their covariance; shared calibration or common external data can make that covariance nonzero. Posterior shapes may also be non-Gaussian or prior-sensitive. A responsible comparison first harmonizes definitions, data cuts, nuisance models and parameterization, then evaluates a difference using joint samples or a justified covariance model. The course summary table deliberately preserves source labels and does not manufacture a combined tension statistic from incomplete marginal errors.",
    "Energy conservation for a homogeneous component with pressure p=w rho gives rho proportional to a^{-3(1+w)} when w is constant. Curvature contributes both to the expansion rate and to the transverse-distance mapping, so changing Omega_k cannot be represented by modifying only H(z). Distances at different redshifts can share degeneracies among curvature, dark-energy behavior and the sound horizon; multiple calibrated probes help break them. Constant w is a low-dimensional test model, not an arbitrary dark-energy history, and its inferred value depends on the assumed early-time contents and priors.",
    "A useful error budget names where uncertainty originates and how it propagates: detector response, photometric calibration, standardization, redshift, selection, population variation and cosmological modeling. Independent noise often averages down; a shared calibration mode does not. Covariance is a mathematical representation of these dependencies, while nuisance parameters can expose physically interpretable uncertainty. Provenance controls another failure mode: unknown units, reordered rows, stale releases or undocumented transformations. A digest confirms which bytes were analyzed, but only tests, source verification and scientific review establish whether those bytes and assumptions are appropriate.",
    "A defensible cosmological claim is a chain: source records, selection, calibration, observable, covariance, forward model, inference, validation and interpretation. At each transition, record units, software, assumptions and what is not represented. An independent implementation or limiting case can expose numerical errors, while posterior predictive or null tests probe model failure. The final statement should separate directly measured quantities from derived values and model-dependent parameters. A complete artifact set is not itself a review verdict; source spot-checks and local policy adaptation remain required before instruction.",
]


